<div class="note">Suspension of sentence — Section 389 CrPC for legacy proceedings, Section 430 BNSS for proceedings under the new code — is interim relief tethered to the appeal: it says nothing about the appeal&rsquo;s eventual outcome, and it stands recalled if the appeal fails. Each application turns on its own record, including the quantity involved and the state of the appellate docket.</div>
